    "IEUvecO5kNM": {
      "result": "awaiting_reconstruction",
      "notes": "All 37 states and narration reviewed; native image 13 establishes a complete sixteen-piece major-piece ending with White Kf4/Qc8/Rf8/Bd3/d4/e3/g3/h4 versus Black Kh6/Qg6/Bg4/d7/e6/f6/g7/h5. The source queen offer is visually Qe4+, despite the caption/transcript saying d4. Two legal-only draft branches reach ...g5+ with fourteen pieces still present. Both allow the ordinary hxg5+ pawn capture from h4, checking Black’s king; neither is immediate mate despite the source assertion. The draft records the actual legal reply rather than accepting the mate language.",
      "analysis_required": "Verify the full sixteen-piece Qe4+ sacrifice and all legal White replies; distinguish visually reconstructed e4 from transcript d4. Check the e5-before-g5 move order and the Kxe4/d5+ intermezzo with every pawn and white rook/queen retained. Actual terminal pawn mates do not certify the larger root or the source claims about rejected queen captures and checking alternatives. Resolve the legal hxg5+ response after ...g5+ in both bishop- and king-capture branches. This is an ordinary pawn capture, not en passant; the White h4 pawn must be retained.",
